      "text": "��<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Transitional//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-transitional.dtd\"><html><body><p><p></p><p><span><b>Generalization</b> occurs when similar experiences are presented to the individual.�</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span>A conditioned response to certain stimuli is established.�</span><span>Other stimuli which are similar will also bring about that response. That is generalization.</span></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"http://image.slidesharecdn.com/behaviorslides1-150311015046-conversion-gate01/95/behavior-learning-classical-conditioning-19-638.jpg?cb=1426038893\" alt=\"\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" role=\"presentation\" class=\"img-responsive atto_image_button_text-bottom\" style=\"font-size: medium;\"></p><p style=\"text-align: left;\"><b>For example</b>, if the cat has been conditioned to meow when she hears the electric can opener, she might also meow when she hears the blender or food processor if she perceives these sounds are similar to the can opener sound.<br></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: right;\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: medium; line-height: 115%;\">�</span></p></p></body></html>",
